      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To start the process, I was feeling really stressed and then I made the decision to go on vacation."
      ],
      "justification": "Covers process initiation, the stated emotional state, and the triggering vacation decision."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n6",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If I decided yes, then I would choose the travel method."
      ],
      "justification": "Opens the first XOR split and captures the positive condition leading to travel method selection."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n4",
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if I decided no, then I would resign from my job."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the negative branch condition and the resulting resignation action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once I resigned from my job, the process would come to an end."
      ],
      "justification": "Matches the first process termination point triggered by resignation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n7",
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If I chose the plane as my travel method, then I would proceed with booking the tickets."
      ],
      "justification": "Opens the second XOR split and captures the plane condition along with ticket booking."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n9",
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "On the other hand, if I chose the car, then I would book a hotel."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the alternative car condition and the hotel booking action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After booking the tickets, they would be successfully booked."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly maps to the ticket booking completion confirmation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Similarly, after booking the hotel, it would be successfully booked as well."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly maps to the hotel booking completion confirmation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n11",
        "action:n12",
        "action:n14",
        "action:n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the luggage was packed, I would take it to the car."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures packing and transporting luggage. Duplicate nodes restating the same steps are harmless redundancy and preserve behaviour."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13",
        "action:n16"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, when the luggage was taken to the car, the process would come to an end."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the second process endpoint. Redundant action nodes do not alter flow or behaviour."
    }
  ],
